/ Title row at the top of a page. The block holds the actions on the right.
/   = render "ui/page_header", title: "Receipts", description: "Photos waiting to be read." do
/     = ui_link_button "Upload", new_receipt_path
- description = local_assigns[:description]
/ A partial always gets a block from Rails, so block_given? is always true here. Without a caller's
/ block, yield returns nothing (blank), and the actions row is left out.
- actions = yield
header.page-header
  .page-header-row
    div
      h1 = title
      - if description
        p.mt-1.text-ink-muted = description
    - if actions.present?
      .page-header-actions
        = actions
